{"from": "text:josephus-war-6-288-300", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-04-01-arrest-captain-sadducees", "grade": "B", "note": "Confirms the institutional setting of the arresting party: the temple watch and its captain, with the priests, stood in Jerusalem in the same period; it does not attest that they arrested Peter and John. Regraded A to B by reviewer 10 when the office claim was split out."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-18-sects", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-04-02-sadducees-upset-resurrection", "grade": "B", "note": "Confirms the setting of the provocation: the Sadducees, the resurrection-denying party, were a real party of the same city and period; it does not attest that they were upset at this preaching. Regraded A to B by reviewer 10 when the doctrine claim was split out."}
